From 4e25714e41a3a608389b7e46b7d9d5d808ce06d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 13:45:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Fill frameless fullscreen client surfaces

Some applications enter borderless fullscreen by removing their frame and
resizing the window in separate WindowPos transitions.  The final fullscreen
transition can therefore retain the previous decorated client rectangle even
though the live style is already frameless.

For own-toplevel client surfaces, that stale rectangle becomes the subsurface
viewport and leaves the former title-bar area transparent.  This is especially
visible with fractional scaling after switching from windowed to borderless
fullscreen.

Once a window is both frameless and classified as fullscreen, its Wayland
presentation client covers the full visible surface.  Keep the underlying
Win32 window rectangles untouched so applications continue to observe their
own window metrics.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
index 588a77c1fff..26bf21f63bb 100644
@@ -233,6 +233,12 @@ static void wayland_win_data_get_config(struct wayland_win_data *data,
         window_state |= WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_MAXIMIZED;
     }
 
+    /* A frame removal and fullscreen resize may arrive in separate WindowPos
+     * updates, leaving the cached client rect with the old frame insets. */
+    if ((window_state & WAYLAND_SURFACE_CONFIG_STATE_FULLSCREEN) &&
+        !(style & (WS_CAPTION | WS_THICKFRAME)))
+        conf->client_rect = conf->rect;
+
     conf->resizeable = (style & WS_THICKFRAME) && !fullscreen;
     conf->state = window_state;
     conf->managed = data->managed;

-- 
